# status: draft (2026-11-05), waiting for the owner's approval
# Things to read around Elderroot (owner request: more to explore): carved stones, signs and notice boards.
# Opened by LoreStone (src/world/places/lore_stone.gd). Short: one look, one thought from Aurelia.
# Only GameState, QuestManager, Inventory, PlayerData, DragonManager, Cutscene and AudioManager may be called.

~ grove_stone
The stone is soft with moss. Under it, someone carved a circle of little lights.
Aurelia: [#thinking] "Where the old lights sleep, the forest remembers." That's from Telwyn's Almanac! Page forty... something.
Aurelia: [#happy] The mushrooms are glowing in a ring. Like the carving. I knew books were useful.
=> END

~ tower_stone
A worn plaque by the broken stairs. Most of the letters have weathered away.
"...WATCH OVER ELDERROOT ...LIGHT THE BEACON IF THE SKY BURNS..."
Aurelia: [#worried] If the sky burns? I hope nobody ever needed to.
=> END

~ falls_stone
Water has polished this stone smooth. A spiral is cut into its face, glowing faintly.
Aurelia: [#thinking] A spiral pointing up... at the cliff. Spirit steps, maybe? Like in the ruins?
Lumen: Some paths only show themselves to a lantern.
=> END

~ camp_orders
A torn sheet nailed to the board, signed with a burnt thumbprint.
"Scouts: watch the north road. Report every Lantern Shrine. The Herald wants the elf village quiet."
Aurelia: [#scared] The Herald? Elderroot? ...I need to tell the Elder about this.
Aurelia: [#determined] After I deal with these tents. Carefully.
=> END

~ farm_sign
"HOLLIN FARM. Wheat, honey and the best scarecrow in the valley."
"PLEASE DO NOT PRACTISE SPELLS ON THE SCARECROW. THIS MEANS YOU, AURELIA."
Aurelia: [#embarrassed] That was ONE time. And he was fine. Mostly fine.
=> END

~ circle_stone
The stones stand in a ring around an old brazier. A line runs along the base of each one, all pointing to the middle.
Aurelia: [#thinking] "Light at the heart, and the circle answers." Answers what, though?
=> END

~ village_notice
The village notice board is crowded with notes.
"LOST: one grey cat, answers to Dumpling. Ask at the mill." "Bram's forge: pots mended, hooks bent, swords NOT sharpened."
"Lantern Shrines are for resting, not for drying socks. — The Elder"
Aurelia: [#happy] Dumpling is on the mill roof again. He always is.
=> END

~ mill_sign
"ELDERROOT MILL. Flour by the sack. Gossip for free."
=> END
